    "updated_at": "2016-07-07T19:46:51Z",
    "body": "Yes, it's a bit of a problem if you want to allow _more_ instead of _less_; you basically have to use `type=\"text\"` instead. But pointing out that we violate the RFC is not convincing enough -- we know that already.\n\nIn your first comment you said\n\n> But some people do recognise them,\n\nAgain I would like to see concrete examples before changing the spec here.\n\n> and the people that don't simply won't enter them.\n\nThis is not correct; they can enter them by mistake, and I think most people (users and developers alike) expect the browser to catch the mistake.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
